<region region-id="212" left="262.77" top="3895.70" width="327.23" height="15.00" align-x="262.77" align-y="3903.70" show-border="false" show-highlight="false" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="inherit" tag="">
<text use-page-width="false" push-down="false" lock-width="true"><p style="Note" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">axial compression D/C, largest Pu / phi Pn,max</p></text>
</region>
<region region-id="213" left="18.00" top="3950.70" width="572.00" height="22.00" align-x="18.00" align-y="3965.70" show-border="false" show-highlight="false" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="inherit" tag="">
<text use-page-width="false" push-down="false" lock-width="true"><p style="Heading 1" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">7. Interaction by strain compatibility (LRFD 5.6.4.5, C5.6.2.1, 5.5.4.2)</p></text>
</region>
<region region-id="214" left="18.00" top="3978.70" width="572.00" height="147.00" align-x="18.00" align-y="3988.70" show-border="false" show-highlight="false" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="inherit" tag="">
<text use-page-width="false" push-down="false" lock-width="true"><p style="List" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">• Strain is linear with the extreme compression fiber at eps_cu = 0.003 and a neutral-axis depth c swept geometrically from 4H to 0.02H (H = depth of the section normal to the bending axis). Strand strain = eps_pe + eps_ce + eps_cu (d - c)/c.</p><p style="List" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">• Strand stress: PCI power formula for Grade 270 low-relaxation strand in tension, Ep eps in compression (no correction for displaced concrete). Concrete: rectangular block a = beta1 c on the compressed part of the square (chamfers ignored).</p><p style="List" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">• Pn is held between -Aps fpy and Pn,max; phi runs from 0.75 to 1.00 as the net tensile strain goes from 0.002 to 0.005. The pure-compression and pure-tension points are scalars; the sweep vectors hold the 121 points between them.</p><p style="List" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">• Figure 2 is a picture; the points behind it are the live vectors of this section (Mathcad recomputes them).</p></text>
</region>
<region region-id="215" left="18.00" top="4133.70" width="133.33" height="20.00" align-x="18.00" align-y="4144.70" show-border="false" show-highlight="false" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="inherit" tag="">
