</region>
<region region-id="460" left="18.00" top="8943.61" width="572.00" height="43.00" align-x="18.00" align-y="8953.61" show-border="false" show-highlight="false" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="inherit" tag="">
<text use-page-width="false" push-down="false" lock-width="true"><p style="Normal" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">The ray meets the sweep between two neighbouring points; the neutral-axis depth there is interpolated. The worksheet takes the notebook&#x27;s depth c_gov as an input, finds the same depth from its own vectors, and evaluates the section exactly at c_gov (no interpolation between sweep points).</p></text>
</region>
<region region-id="461" left="18.00" top="8992.61" width="175.21" height="17.00" align-x="18.00" align-y="9003.61" show-border="false" show-highlight="true" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="#ffff80" tag="">
