</region>
<region region-id="716" left="41.12" top="14002.01" width="525.75" height="142.50" align-x="41.12" align-y="14002.01" show-border="false" show-highlight="true" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="#ececec" tag="">
<plot disable-calc="false" item-idref="3"/>
</region>
<region region-id="717" left="18.00" top="14152.51" width="572.00" height="38.50" align-x="18.00" align-y="14161.01" show-border="false" show-highlight="false" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="inherit" tag="">
<text use-page-width="false" push-down="false" lock-width="true"><p style="Note" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">Figure 3. Demand/capacity ratio of each distilled check (stems) against the limit (dashed line). It is a Mathcad plot of CheckGood and CheckNoGood, so it recalculates with the worksheet and a check turns red when its ratio passes 1.0.</p></text>
</region>
<region region-id="718" left="18.00" top="14199.01" width="572.00" height="38.50" align-x="18.00" align-y="14207.51" show-border="false" show-highlight="false" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="inherit" tag="">
<text use-page-width="false" push-down="false" lock-width="true"><p style="Note" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">Check numbers: 1 axial compression; 2 axial + biaxial flexure, 5.6.4.5; 3 axial + flexure, resultant axis; 4 shear; 5 tension; 6 Service I compression; 7 Service I tension; 8 effective prestress; 9 driving strength; 10 minimum size; 11 pile spacing; 12 bearing resistance vs Table 3.5.13-1.</p></text>
</region>
<region region-id="719" left="0" top="14240.51" width="6000" height="6" align-x="0" align-y="14240.51" show-border="false" show-highlight="false" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="inherit" tag="">
<pageBreak/>
</region>
<region region-id="720" left="18.00" top="14252.51" width="572.00" height="73.00" align-x="18.00" align-y="14261.01" show-border="false" show-highlight="false" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="inherit" tag="">
<text use-page-width="false" push-down="false" lock-width="true"><p style="Note" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">The notebook lists 15 PENDING items; the distilled ratios below do not close them: Axial compression · maximum Pu / φPn,max; Axial + biaxial flexure · LRFD Eq. 5.6.4.5-3; Axial + flexure · resultant bending axis (strain compatibility); Shear · general procedure; Service I concrete tension; Minimum square pile size (Table 3.5.1-1); Pile-to-cap moment transfer (embedment below 48 in); Pile Data Table completeness (SDM 11.4); Environment classification; Pile-to-cap connection (12 in embedment); Downdrag source documented; FBMP export current; Minimum tip elevation; Scour resistance and elevations; Drivability.</p></text>
</region>
<region region-id="721" left="18.00" top="14331.51" width="572.00" height="27.00" align-x="18.00" align-y="14340.01" show-border="false" show-highlight="false" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="inherit" tag="">
<text use-page-width="false" push-down="false" lock-width="true"><p style="Note" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">FB-MultiPier reports a largest model D/C of 0.46 at combo 2 STRENGTH-III · pile 4 · element 12J · EL 18.60 ft. The distilled Status covers the recomputed numerical checks only; it is not design acceptance.</p></text>
</region>
<region region-id="722" left="18.00" top="14364.51" width="572.00" height="50.00" align-x="18.00" align-y="14373.01" show-border="false" show-highlight="false" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="inherit" tag="">
<text use-page-width="false" push-down="false" lock-width="true"><p style="Note" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">Notebook values for comparison, D/C: axial compression 0.137; axial + biaxial flexure, 5.6.4.5 0.474; axial + flexure, resultant axis 0.398; shear 0.074; tension 0.000; Service I compression 0.550; Service I tension 0.000; effective prestress 0.675; driving strength 0.769; minimum size 0.778; pile spacing 1.000; bearing resistance vs Table 3.5.13-1 0.300; largest 1.000.</p></text>
</region>
</regions>
